<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indus Valley Civilisation</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus-valley">Indus Valley</a> Civilisation was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> civilisation in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> basin, known for planned cities such as Harappa and Mohenjo-daro. It is generally identified with the land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meluhha">Meluhha</a> in Mesopotamian texts. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> traded with it by sea through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indus-valley-civilisation.jpg" alt="Indus Valley Civilisation" width="320" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avantiputra7 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Indus_Valley_Civilization,_Mature_Phase_(2600-1900_BCE).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
